[2026-03-14T22:05:49.615Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NfuZxN2GgE4LvAYxWUoW7F","type":"tool_result","content":"  1113→\n  1114→#### Test: Sidebar renders all property fields\n  1115→- **Initial state**: User is on the issue detail page for an issue with status \"In Progress\", priority \"High\", assignee \"Alice\", labels [\"Bug\", \"Frontend\"], project \"Auth Rewrite\", cycle \"Sprint 3\", due date \"2026-04-01\"\n  1116→- **Expected**: The right sidebar displays all property fields: Status showing \"In Progress\" with half-circle yellow icon, Priority showing \"High\" with orange arrow-up icon, Assignee showing \"Alice\" with avatar, Labels showing \"Bug\" and \"Frontend\" as colored badges, Project showing \"Auth Rewrite\", Cycle showing \"Sprint 3\", Due Date showing \"Apr 1, 2026\", Created timestamp (read-only), and Updated timestamp (read-only).\n  1117→\n  1118→#### Test: Change status via sidebar dropdown\n  1119→- **Initial state**: Issue has status \"Todo\". User is on the issue detail page.\n  1120→- **Action**: User clicks the Status field in the sidebar\n  1121→- **Expected**: A dropdown appears listing all statuses (Backlog, Todo, In Progress, In Review, Done, Cancelled) with their respective icons and colors.\n  1122→\n  1123→#### Test: Select new status in sidebar\n  1124→- **Initial state**: The status dropdown is open in the sidebar, current status is \"Todo\"\n  1125→- **Action**: User clicks \"Done\"\n  1126→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes. Status updates to \"Done\" with a green check-circle icon. The change is persisted. An activity entry is created. The inline status selector in the header also updates to \"Done\".\n  1127→\n  1128→#### Test: Change priority via sidebar dropdown\n  1129→- **Initial state**: Issue has priority \"Medium\". User is on the issue detail page.\n  1130→- **Action**: User clicks the Priority field in the sidebar\n  1131→- **Expected**: A dropdown appears listing all priorities (Urgent, High, Medium, Low, No Priority) with their respective icons and colors.\n  1132→\n  1133→#### Test: Select new priority in sidebar\n  1134→- **Initial state**: The priority dropdown is open, current priority is \"Medium\"\n  1135→- **Action**: User clicks \"Urgent\"\n  1136→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes. Priority updates to \"Urgent\" with a red alert-triangle icon. The change is persisted. An activity entry is created recording the priority change from \"Medium\" to \"Urgent\".\n  1137→\n  1138→#### Test: Change assignee via searchable selector\n  1139→- **Initial state**: Issue is unassigned. The workspace has members \"Alice\", \"Bob\", and \"Charlie\".\n  1140→- **Action**: User clicks the Assignee field in the sidebar\n  1141→- **Expected**: A searchable dropdown appears showing all workspace members with their avatars and names.\n  1142→\n  1143→#### Test: Search and select assignee\n  1144→- **Initial state**: The assignee dropdown is open showing all members\n  1145→- **Action**: User types \"Ali\" in the search field\n  1146→- **Expected**: The list filters to show only \"Alice\". User clicks \"Alice\".\n  1147→- **Action**: User clicks \"Alice\"\n  1148→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes. Assignee updates to show Alice's avatar and name. The change is persisted. An activity entry is created. A notification is sent to Alice that she was assigned to this issue.\n  1149→\n  1150→#### Test: Remove assignee\n  1151→- **Initial state**: Issue is assigned to \"Alice\"\n  1152→- **Action**: User clicks the Assignee field, then clicks an \"Unassign\" or clear option\n  1153→- **Expected**: The assignee is removed. The field shows as unassigned (e.g., \"No assignee\" or empty avatar placeholder). The change is persisted. An activity entry is created.\n  1154→\n  1155→#### Test: Add labels via multi-select picker\n  1156→- **Initial state**: Issue has no labels. Available labels include \"Bug\" (red), \"Feature\" (green), \"Improvement\" (blue).\n  1157→- **Action**: User clicks the Labels field in the sidebar\n  1158→- **Expected**: A multi-select dropdown appears showing all available labels with their colored dots and names. No labels are checked.\n  1159→\n  1160→#### Test: Select multiple labels\n  1161→- **Initial state**: The labels picker is open, no labels selected\n  1162→- **Action**: User clicks \"Bug\", then clicks \"Frontend\"\n  1163→- **Expected**: Both \"Bug\" and \"Frontend\" are checked in the dropdown. The sidebar field updates to show both labels as colored badges. The changes are persisted. Activity entries are created for each label addition.\n  1164→\n  1165→#### Test: Remove a label\n  1166→- **Initial state**: Issue has labels \"Bug\" and \"Frontend\". The labels picker is open.\n  1167→- **Action**: User unchecks \"Bug\"\n  1168→- **Expected**: \"Bug\" is removed from the issue. Only \"Frontend\" badge remains in the sidebar. The change is persisted. An activity entry is created recording the label removal.\n  1169→\n  1170→#### Test: Change project via searchable selector\n  1171→- **Initial state**: Issue has no project assigned. Available projects include \"Auth Rewrite\", \"Performance Optimization\", \"Mobile App\".\n  1172→- **Action**: User clicks the Project field in the sidebar\n  1173→- **Expected**: A searchable dropdown appears listing available projects.\n  1174→\n  1175→#### Test: Search and select project\n  1176→- **Initial state**: The project dropdown is open\n  1177→- **Action**: User types \"Auth\" in the search field, then clicks \"Auth Rewrite\"\n  1178→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes. Project updates to show \"Auth Rewrite\". The change is persisted. An activity entry is created.\n  1179→\n  1180→#### Test: Remove project assignment\n  1181→- **Initial state**: Issue is assigned to project \"Auth Rewrite\"\n  1182→- **Action**: User clicks the Project field, then clicks a \"Remove\" or clear option\n  1183→- **Expected**: The project is unassigned. The field shows as empty (e.g., \"No project\"). The change is persisted. An activity entry is created.\n  1184→\n  1185→#### Test: Change cycle via dropdown\n  1186→- **Initial state**: Issue belongs to team \"Engineering\" which has cycles \"Sprint 2\" (completed), \"Sprint 3\" (active), \"Sprint 4\" (upcoming). Issue has no cycle assigned.\n  1187→- **Action**: User clicks the Cycle field in the sidebar\n  1188→- **Expected**: A dropdown appears showing available cycles for the team: \"Sprint 2\", \"Sprint 3\", \"Sprint 4\" with their date ranges.\n  1189→\n  1190→#### Test: Select cycle\n  1191→- **Initial state**: The cycle dropdown is open\n  1192→- **Action**: User clicks \"Sprint 3\"\n  1193→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes. Cycle updates to show \"Sprint 3\". The change is persisted. An activity entry is created.\n  1194→\n  1195→#### Test: Change due date via date picker\n  1196→- **Initial state**: Issue has no due date set\n  1197→- **Action**: User clicks the Due Date field in the sidebar\n  1198→- **Expected**: A date picker opens allowing the user to select a date.\n  1199→\n  1200→#### Test: Select due date\n  1201→- **Initial state**: The date picker is open\n  1202→- **Action**: User selects April 15, 2026\n  1203→- **Expected**: The date picker closes. Due Date updates to show \"Apr 15, 2026\". The change is persisted. An activity entry is created.\n  1204→\n  1205→#### Test: Clear due date\n  1206→- **Initial state**: Issue has due date \"Apr 15, 2026\"\n  1207→- **Action**: User clicks the Due Date field and clicks a \"Clear\" or remove option\n  1208→- **Expected**: The due date is removed. The field shows as empty (e.g., \"No due date\"). The change is persisted. An activity entry is created.\n  1209→\n  1210→#### Test: Created and Updated timestamps are read-only\n  1211→- **Initial state**: User is on the issue detail page. The issue was created on \"Mar 10, 2026\" and last updated \"Mar 14, 2026\".\n  1212→- **Expected**: The Created field shows \"Mar 10, 2026\" (or relative time like \"4 days ago\") and the Updated field shows \"Mar 14, 2026\" (or \"today\"). Both fields are not clickable/editable — they have no hover cursor change or click handler.\n  1213→\n  1214→#### Test: Sidebar dropdowns close on outside click\n  1215→- **Initial state**: The priority dropdown is open in the sidebar\n  1216→- **Action**: User clicks outside the dropdown (e.g., on the description area)\n  1217→- **Expected**: The dropdown closes without changing the priority value.\n  1218→\n  1219→#### Test: Use assignee selector multiple times in sequence\n  1220→- **Initial state**: Issue is assigned to \"Alice\"\n  1221→- **Action**: User clicks the Assignee field, selects \"Bob\", then immediately clicks the Assignee field again and selects \"Charlie\"\n  1222→- **Expected**: The assignee correctly updates to \"Charlie\" after the second selection. Both changes create separate activity entries. The search input resets between uses."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LWKe4w7qgjRFh9ZN9qttZa","session_id":"677438e1-1261-4d5a-9849-a62a9293ba3b","uuid":"03fa7f3f-1e6e-44f2-908a-7c71932a3f7f"}
